  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nSurface high pressure will build to our southwest today,\nallowing for mainly sunny skies with high temperatures into the\nupper 70s/lower 80s across the north with middle to upper 80s\nsouth of the mountains. Daytime mixing will allow for\ncomfortable humidity values with dew points mainly into the 50s.\nIt will be a bit breezy as well with westerly wind gusts up to\naround 25 mph at times, especially through the first half of the\nday.\n\nClear to partly cloudy skies tonight combined with light winds\nwill allow temperatures to cool to around 50 degrees across some\ninterior valleys with upper 50s to lower 60s elsewhere.\n\nThe warming trend will continue on Wednesday through the\nremainder of the week as a Bermuda High allows for sub-tropical\nair to be transported northward as south-southwesterly flow\nprevails at the surface. This will allow for typical August\nweather with high temperatures each day into the 80s to near 90\ndegrees and elevated dew points into the 60s to near 70 degrees\nat times. The peak of the heat and humidity currently looks to\nbe on Friday when afternoon heat indices may approach the \nmiddle 90s across some interior locations south of the \nmountains. \n\nAs is often the case in the Summer, we will need to watch for \ndiurnally driven showers and thunderstorms most days. While no \nparticular day currently looks overly supportive for severe \nstorms, depending on the timing of a few weak waves of energy, \na few strong to severe storms cannot be ruled out, especially \ntowards late week or this upcoming weekend.",
